    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **James Wood** (74.97) and **Seiya Suzuki** (74.68) headline the squad, leveraging elite matchups against pitchers with high-xERA profiles (Adrian Houser and Sugano, respectively). **James Wood** is our primary engine today; while his park factor is slightly negative, his 0.404 xwOBA and the leadoff spot provide the highest floor-to-ceiling ratio on the board. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost, anchoring our outfield in a favorable hitting environment. **Josh Naylor** (75.66) rounds out our top-tier plays, as favorable wind conditions and a solid matchup against Rogers elevate his value, making him an essential start at 1B.\n\nThe most difficult decision on our bench was **Kyle Karros** (51.87), who narrowly missed the cutoff. While **Kyle Karros** benefits from a strong park factor and a 4.31-xERA opponent, the decision to bench him was purely mathematical; his scoring efficiency currently trails **Gabriel Moreno** and **Vinnie Pasquantino**, whose roles in the middle of their respective lineups provide more consistent counting-stat opportunities. We are also monitoring a 43% rain risk for **Travis Bazzana** (61.46) and a 38% risk for **Zach McKinstry** (43.91). While **Travis Bazzana** remains a strong play due to his leadoff spot, any pre-game delay could force a pivot. Note that **Max Muncy**, **Brice Turang**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **James Wood** are all awaiting final lineup confirmations; should any be dropped from the order, we will be forced to activate secondary options from our depth chart.",
